Z||000000||Raydar||12-02-2000||04:15 PM||||This may have already been covered. <BR>The December issue of Motor Trend has, at the very top of the front cover, <BR>"First Drive: GM's Fast, Fun, Affordable Roadster."<BR>It's a road test of the Opel Speedster.<BR>In the article... "Pontiac and Saturn have both discussed the possibilities of US importation. ...It doesn't hurt that Pontiac product-types reportedly like the styling as is."<BR>The author wrote, "If given a green light, we'd like to see the Fiero moniker brought back to life for the Speedster, with a turbocharged variant to wear a GT badge."<BR>(We do have advocates at Motor Trend.)<P>There is also an opinion poll at motortrend.com.<P>FYI... The Speedster is 1941 lbs. with 147 HP. They estimate 0-60 in 5.9.<P>Raydar||||reg||4
